      {
         "id": "SECTION_poem",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Poems\n\nWhen writing a poem, the author may choose between free composition and adherence to a metrical structure (<htcite0>).\n\n#### Defining Meter\n\nIf a specific meter is selected, each verse of the poem must contain the same number of metrical syllables. Note that metrical conventions vary across languages. For simplicity, this text adopts the definitions and examples of Portuguese. Readers who wish to compare them may consult the article on meter published by the University of Pennsylvania (<htcite1>).\n\nIn Portuguese, metrical syllables are counted up to the last stressed syllable—the most emphatically pronounced syllable—rather than up to the total number of syllables in a verse (<htcite2>).\n\nThe poem *\"Voltas\"* consists of 5-syllable verses, known in Portuguese as *redondilhas menores* (<htcite3>). Below we reproduce that text (<htcite4>):",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "bde4985f-01f0-4cda-8018-2f463970d9a5",
                     "text": "Goldstein, N. S.",
                     "page": "pp. 5",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "1985",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "560ca1c7-f50f-47ae-a7df-ec91e3082b65",
                     "text": "Encyclopedia of poetry and poetics",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "1965",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 0,
                     "uuid": "f31a3b93-d7f8-411e-8e82-bbd0464659fd",
                     "text": "Academia das Ciências de Lisboa",
                     "page": "redondilha",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "",
                        "year": "",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "e19e9e01-3403-4140-b9b6-90a4b9a21229",
                     "text": "Camões, Luís Vaz de.",
                     "page": "pp. 19",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "",
                        "year": "",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "52e35c58-b0e7-49d1-a719-1feaee3773f8",
                     "text": "Arruda Franco, M.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2017",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<ul class=\"citation\"><li><i><b>Voltas</b></i></li><li><i>&nbsp;</i></li> <li><i>Da lindeza vossa,</i></li> <li><i>Dama, quem a vê,</i></li> <li><i>impossível é</i></li> <li><i>que guardar-se possa.</i></li> <li><i>Se faz tanta mossa</i></li> <li><i>ver-vos um só dia,</i></li> <li><i>quem se guardaria?</i></li> <li><i>&nbsp;</i></li> <li><i>Milhor deve ser</i></li> <li><i>neste aventurar,</i></li> <li><i>ver, e não guardar,</i></li> <li><i>que guardar de ver.</i></li> <li><i>Ver, e defender,</i></li> <li><i>muito bom seria;</i></li> <li><i>mas... quem poderia?</i></li> </ul>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "#### The Multiplication Table of *Voltas*\n\nBefore analyzing the poem’s syllables, let us highlight key features:\n\n- Each verse (line) of *Voltas* contains exactly 5 Portuguese metrical syllables.\n- Each strophe — a group of verses separated by a blank line (<htcite0>) — comprises 7 verses.\n- The poem contains two strophes.\n\nGiven this structure, the total number of metrical syllables can be calculated in three different ways:",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "bde4985f-01f0-4cda-8018-2f463970d9a5",
                     "text": "Goldstein, N. S.",
                     "page": "pp. 24 - 25",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "1985",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\" style=\"background-color: #FFFFFF;\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\" style=\"background-color: #FFFFFF;\">\n\n**1. Individual syllables: add 1 for each of the 70 syllables**: <math mathsize=\"1.5em\" displaystyle=\"false\"><munderover><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>70</mn></mrow></munderover><mi>1</mi><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">=</mo><mi>1 × (70)</mi><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">=</mo><mi>70</mi></math>\n\n**2. Per strophe: 7 verses × 5 syllables**: <math mathsize=\"1.5em\" displaystyle=\"false\"><munderover><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></munderover><mi>5</mi><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">=</mo><mi>7 × (5)</mi><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">=</mo><mi>35</mi></math>.\n\n*Each strophe gives 7 × 5 = 35 syllables. With two strophes we double that result:* 35 + 35 = 2 × (35) = 70\n\n**3. Across all verses: 14 verses × 5 syllables**: <math mathsize=\"1.5em\" displaystyle=\"false\"><munderover><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow></munderover><mi>5</mi><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">=</mo><mi>14 × (5)</mi><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">=</mo><mi>70</mi></math>\n\n*All three methods give the same total: 70 syllables. The third method will be explored in detail in another text.*</div></div></center>\n\n#### Verse Chart\n\nBecause every verse contains the same number of metrical syllables (5), all the points of the graph sit at the same height, producing a flat, horizontal line:",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htChart\"><canvas aria-label=\"chart\" id=\"chart2\" style=\"width:30em !important; height:20em !important;\"></canvas></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Chart 2</b>: Metrical syllables per verse in <i>Voltas</i>. Chart created with the <htcite0> library.</div></p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "6efe7632-faed-4080-a5aa-38463d43e6d7",
                     "text": "Chart JS",
                     "page": "",
