      {
         "id": "SECTION_hieroglyphics",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### The Mathematics in Hieroglyphics\n\nIn addition to the alphabets we use today, humanity has also developed different writing systems (<htcite0>), where mathematics is likewise present.\n\n#### The Mesoamerican Texts\n\nLooking at **Figure 1**, which shows part of Stela A located in the archaeological site of Copán, Honduras, we can observe two columns of hieroglyphs displayed in nine lines on the stela's side.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "5390fa3b-735f-4e22-ac98-178303a13fdb",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "The Writing System",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"imgCopanStelaA\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgCopanStelaA', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\" style=\"width:30%\"/><b>Figure 1</b>: Stela A at the Copán Archaeological Museum, featuring inscriptions referencing Copán, Tikal, Calakmul, and Palenque in sequence (<htcite0>). Photo taken on <htdate1> during a visit to the site.</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "1e007481-9bd3-4a09-ad4d-6e812fe79641",
                     "text": "Instituto Hondureño de Antropologia e Historia",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "02",
                        "day": "01"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2024",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  },
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2015",
                     "month": "7",
                     "day": "30"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "This image displays a hieroglyphic text arranged in two columns.",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "Counting hieroglyphs follows the same logic as counting metrical syllables in verses: each line carries a fixed number of signs. Thus, **Figure 1** shows a total of 18 hieroglyphs (2 columns × 9 lines = 18).\n\n#### Chart of Hieroglyphs\n\nIn **Chart 3** we plot the number of hieroglyphs per line. Compared with **Chart 2**, we again see a constant quantity: every point has the value 2 instead of the value 5 of the previous chart.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htChart\"><canvas aria-label=\"chart\" id=\"chart3\" style=\"width:30em !important; height:20em !important;\"></canvas></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Chart 3</b>: Hieroglyphics per line in Stela A. Chart created by <htcite0>.</div></p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "6efe7632-faed-4080-a5aa-38463d43e6d7",
                     "text": "Chart JS",
                     "page": "",
